# Netlify response headers for the CRM.
#
# Keep search engines out of crm.skybluecleaningco.com entirely.
#
# The CRM is behind a login, with one deliberate exception: the public quote
# page at /q/<token>. That token is 64 random hex characters, so nothing can
# guess or crawl its way to one — but a customer who shares their quote link
# somewhere public would put their own name, address and price into Google's
# index, and there is no way to take that back quickly.
#
# Why this rather than a robots.txt "Disallow":
#
#   Disallow stops a crawler READING the page, not indexing the URL. Google
#   will still list a disallowed URL it has seen linked from elsewhere — it
#   just shows the bare address with no description. Worse, having been told
#   not to fetch the page, it can never see a noindex instruction inside it.
#
#   X-Robots-Tag works the other way round: crawlers are allowed to fetch,
#   and what they fetch tells them not to index. That is the one that
#   actually keeps a leaked quote link out of search results.
#
# So there is deliberately NO robots.txt in this project. Adding one with a
# Disallow rule would undo this by making the header unreadable.
#
# Applies to every response Netlify serves from this site, including the
# paths rewritten to index.html by _redirects.

/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
